Pad button remapping: support comma-separated button sources for multi-slot bindings. In the PC options overlay, controller mapping allows both primary and secondary slots to be bound to physical buttons for each game action. BitForName previously only matched single button names, returning 0 if a cvar contained multiple buttons separated by commas (e.g. "a,lb"). BitForName now parses comma-separated tokens and returns the bitwise OR of all matched button masks, allowing multiple physical controller buttons to trigger the same game action.

